A command calling a package's Broken, which holds a type error and carries a record
naming DS1001. The call is outside Broken's body, so the type error hides no use
of Broken: no finding about it can carry DS1001 and the record is stale.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}}
-- main.go --
package main

import "example.com/app/lib"

func main() { lib.Broken() }
-- lib/lib.go --
package lib

//deadset:ignore DS1001 -- kept for the loader
func Broken() int { return undefinedName }
